    "title": "V 得/不得",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk5-potential-r5-01-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "V 得/不得",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "After the verb, the potential form evaluates whether an action is feasible or acceptable in this situation. Contrast a prohibition placed before the verb. The negative potential complement has its own intended reading. Preverbal 不得 bùdé is a formal prohibition; postverbal 不得 bude describes an infeasible or unacceptable action. They differ in syntax and reading.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "这件事做不得。",
                "pinyin": "zhè jiàn shì zuò bude 。",
                "meaning": "This is not something we can acceptably do.",
                "audio": "53d03fef513cc7e9a190b314a7ddd215b6e57dfcb11e2af1bfbd36ea13400a26"
              },
              {
                "text": "这里不得停车。",
                "pinyin": "zhèlǐ bùdé tíngchē 。",
                "meaning": "Parking is prohibited here.",
                "audio": "64c06aeeb810c9826155d026de629a3b203cb67171468521c17fc640b41cacdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Words used in this pattern",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "得",
                "pinyin": "de",
                "meaning": "links an action to an achievable result or direction",
